components.what:
C1 Wire tap in the statusline. Add rate_limits.five_hour and rate_limits.seven_day (used_percentage, resets_at) to the jq @tsv call that already runs, and carry them in the /tmp/cc-telemetry row. Using bash builtins only:
(a) keep a per-config ledger ~/.reso/limit-recover/wire/<cfgbase>.json that stores only the MAX reading per resets_at, rewritten only when the integer percent rises;
(b) create one O_EXCL marker per (cfgbase, window, resets_at, band) in ~/.reso/limit-recover/wire/ev/. Bands are 5h>=90/95 and 7d>=90/95/98. A 'deadline' marker is written when seven_day.resets_at - now <= 6h and used <= 95.

Landing band. A new cache-only `claude-accounts --rebal-band --json` gives one row per account:
- weekly used %, hours to reset, and pace lo/hi (burn_wk_ewma_ph, burn_wk_flat_ph);
- projected landing L = used + pace_hi x reset_h;
- raw strand (wk_strand_pp) and the same strand minus that horizon's measured nowcast bias (interpolated from the --strand-score table);
- weekly wall ETA at pace_hi;
- sink capacity in pp/h = (100 - margin - L)/reset_h;
- 5-hour landing and capacity from burn_5h_ewma_ph.
Verdicts: sink | donor-7d | donor-5h | neutral | walled | unknown:*. A sink may open at any horizon up to 96h once its corrected strand is at least STRAND_SCORE_FLOOR (4 pp). A large strand therefore opens early and a small one late.

Event-driven scheduling. The controller starts on:
- every new account-utilization.jsonl sample (launchd WatchPaths, ThrottleInterval 60);
- a weekly reset roll, so the conveyor advances to the next sink;
- a StopFailure rate_limit marker, to re-plan targets (the walled cohort itself stays the reconciler's).
lrp_shed_kick stays as the 9-min backstop. Batches are filed with --until-idle up to the next expected tick, so component 5 catches the end of a turn.

Acceptance ledger: `lr-balance --report`. For each weekly window it reports:
- final landing and strand pp;
- pp burned on sinks by rebal-moved sessions (component 2, after the move);
- walls and wall session-hours, counting *.jsonl.handed-off so walls are not credited to the destination account;
- moves, casualties and pane-outage seconds;
- warm-cache cost, ctx x (WRITE_PP - READ_PP).
